From 4500af9a7152e1999af9f24250e38867c7fd5b56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott <158021536+nathawatc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:48:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vision): pin DNN engine by OpenCV version and filter
 target warning (#21)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## What

- Pin the DNN engine by OpenCV version. 5.1 removed the Classic engine
and renumbered the engine enum, so `OPENCV_FORCE_DNN_ENGINE=2` now
selects ONNX Runtime. Howdy now sets `ENGINE_NEW` on 5.0 and
`ENGINE_OPENCV` on 5.1+, with the value taken from the enum.
- Filter OpenCV's false-positive warning "Targets are not supported by
the new graph engine for now" on OpenCV 5.0.0 through 5.1.0.
opencv/opencv#29457 fixed it, but opencv/opencv#29286 brought it back
for builds without CUDA before 5.1.0 was tagged. The upstream fix for
that regression, opencv/opencv#30808, is under review; if merged, it
should ship in the next OpenCV release after 5.1.0. The filter drops
only that exact message; every other OpenCV log message still prints
unchanged. It stays permanently for 5.0.0 through 5.1.0, since those
releases always print the warning.
- Docs: `howdy/src/vision/AGENTS.md` records the SFace drift between 5.0
and 5.1 and points to #2 for upstream status instead of duplicating it.

## Validation

- Real YuNet/SFace models, 5.0 vs 5.1: preprocessing and YuNet detection
are bit-identical. SFace embeddings differ (cosine 0.988–0.998 for the
same input); match scores moved by at most 0.03 with no threshold
crossings.
- End to end on 5.0.0 and 5.1.0: the target warning is gone, and other
OpenCV warnings (`imread`, ONNX Runtime fallback) still print.
- Local debug build on OpenCV 5.0.0: 109/109.

## Notes

- Split from #17, which was closed when its branch was renamed. The Nix
OpenCV 5.1.0 bump moved to a separate draft PR so NixOS users are not
moved to 5.1 before a hardware test.
- Nix stays on OpenCV 5.0.0 and CI image `ci-nix:2.35.3-1`.

